  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1141 AM MST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nWeather will remain dry the rest of this week, with temperatures \nwarming a few degrees on Thursday. Upper ridge overhead will remain \nin place until Saturday, when a wave will pass through and bring \nsome high based showers to the Continental Divide. Light snow \naccumulations are expected throughout Saturday Night, with rain \nshowers spreading to the eastern plains Sunday morning.\n\nThe wave will move on pretty quickly, with the area drying out again \nlater Sunday into Monday. Model solutions quickly diverge further in \nthe future, though recent trends suggest another broad trough moving \ninto our region by the middle of next week, bringing in a cooler and \nmore active pattern for our area.",
